## What C gives up

- **C is still short duration, but within a loss limit.** Spread-bearing assets here are shorter than the liabilities, and long Treasuries carry zero spread. So the optimizer runs a short position (surplus DV01 {{phase5.portfolios.C.surplus_dv01_k|+.1f}}k per bp) up to the −100bp scenario limit of {{inputs.scenario_max_loss|.2f}}.
  - A 100bp fall changes C's surplus by **{{phase5.stress.C_parallel_down_100_dS|+.2f}}**, against {{phase5.stress.A_parallel_down_100_dS|+.2f}} for A. A 100bp rise changes it by {{phase5.stress.C_parallel_up_100_dS|+.2f}}.
  - Holding that limit costs {{phase6.constraints.scenario_cost|.4f}} a year of income, versus an unconstrained C at {{phase6.constraints.dS_parallel_down_100_C_before|+.2f}}.
- **C has more credit and spread risk.** NAIC 3+ spreads +200bp change C's surplus by {{phase5.stress.C_hy_spread_up_200_dS|+.2f}}, against {{phase5.stress.A_hy_spread_up_200_dS|+.2f}} for A and {{phase5.stress.B_hy_spread_up_200_dS|+.2f}} for B. C holds {{phase5.portfolios.C.hy|.1f}} of NAIC 3+ assets (including CLO BB), {{phase5.portfolios.C.clo|.1f}} of CLOs and {{phase5.portfolios.C.structured_ex_agency|.1f}} of non-agency structured.
- **Capital is sized to a downgrade, not just to today.** Budget utilization is {{phase5.portfolios.C.budget_utilization|.0%}}. The binding row is the downgrade buffer: after a one-notch downgrade of every BBB-family holding, capital is {{phase6.stress.C_bbb_downgrade_one_notch_capital_charge|.3f}}, against a limit of {{report.downgrade_buffer_limit|.2f}}. The buffer costs {{phase6.constraints.buffer_cost|.4f}} a year.
- **The same downgrade breaks the HY limit.** It lifts NAIC 3+ holdings to {{phase6.stress.C_bbb_downgrade_one_notch_hy_after|.1f}} (limit {{inputs.limits.hy_max|.0f}}), because BBB− becomes 3.A. The buffer controls capital, not the HY count.
- **Negative convexity.** C holds {{phase5.portfolios.C.agency_mbs|.1f}} of Agency MBS, with effective convexity of about {{phase6.mbs.FNMA_30Y_rate_dependent_effective_conv|.0f}} (FNMA). A ±100bp move changes surplus by {{phase4.portfolio_C.dS_full_parallel_up_100|+.2f}} / {{phase4.portfolio_C.dS_full_parallel_down_100|+.2f}}, against {{phase4.portfolio_C.dS_krd_parallel_up_100|+.2f}} / {{phase4.portfolio_C.dS_krd_parallel_down_100|+.2f}} on a linear estimate.
- **Combined adverse stress** (−100bp, wider spreads, BBB downgrades): C {{phase6.stress.C_combined_adverse_dS|+.2f}} (it was {{phase6.constraints.dS_combined_adverse_C_before|+.2f}} before the scenario limits), B {{phase6.stress.B_combined_adverse_dS|+.2f}}, A {{phase6.stress.A_combined_adverse_dS|+.2f}}.
- **C has the liquidity A lacks.** With surrenders +{{inputs.scenarios.lapse_increase|.0%}} in years 1–5, C's minimum funding balance stays at {{phase6.stress.C_surrenders_up_50pct_y1_5_min_funding_y1_to_check|+.2f}}, while A's falls to {{phase6.stress.A_surrenders_up_50pct_y1_5_min_funding_y1_to_check|+.2f}}.

